theory.intro:
A **quadratic model** uses a parabola to describe a real situation. The vertex gives the largest or smallest value, the intercepts mark the start and the finish, and only part of the parabola makes sense in context.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[-{Stealth}] (-0.4,0) -- (6.4,0) node[right] {time};
\draw[-{Stealth}] (0,-0.4) -- (0,4.4) node[above] {height};
\draw[thick,blue!70!black,domain=0:5.458,samples=100,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{0.9+1.8*\x-0.36*\x*\x});
\fill (0,0.9) circle (2pt);
\fill (2.5,3.15) circle (2pt);
\fill (5.458,0) circle (2pt);
\node[right] at (2.65,3.35) {vertex: greatest height};
\node[right] at (0.2,0.5) {starting height};
\node[below] at (5.458,-0.15) {lands};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

foundation.question_text:
A ball is thrown upwards from the ground.
Its height $h$ metres after $t$ seconds is modelled by $h=-5t^{2}+30t$, and the graph is shown.
Find the maximum height of the ball and the time at which it occurs.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[width=7.5cm,height=7cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=-0.5,xmax=7,ymin=-5,ymax=52,xtick={0,1,...,6},ytick={0,5,...,50},grid=both,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\scriptsize,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={$t$},ylabel={$h$}]
\addplot[thick,blue!70!black,domain=0:6,samples=100] {-5*x*x+30*x};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

