mastery.question_text:
A ball is thrown upwards from the top of a $25$ m cliff.
Its height $h$ metres above the sea after $t$ seconds is modelled by $h=-5t^{2}+20t+25$, and the full parabola is shown.
State the values of $t$ for which the model makes sense, and explain what the rest of the parabola would mean.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
